---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import Scribble from "@/components/Scribble.astro";

const title = "About the Vibe Coding Project";
const description = "The story of a coding outsider finding order in the jungle.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="app-layout py-24">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <header class="mb-16">
        <div class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.4em] text-accent-dim uppercase mb-6 font-bold">THE PROLOGUE</div>
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-serif italic text-ink tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-8">
          Stop <Scribble type="circle">Copying.</Scribble> <br/> Start Commanding.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-text-secondary font-serif italic leading-relaxed">
          "The age of copy-paste is dead. This is the story of how I stopped being a slave to the slop and started building real products."
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-ink max-w-none font-serif text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <strong>June 24, 2025.</strong> Anthropic shipped Claude Code. I'd been messing with AI code tools before that, but this was a different planet.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before Claude Code, my days looked like a repetitive loop of ChatGPT, copy, paste, error, repeat. I was hunting bugs through 10,000 lines of tangled spaghetti with zero coding background.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then I found the <Scribble type="underline">Warden</Scribble> mindset. Stop asking for code. Start defining boundaries. Start using the terminal.
        </p>
        <p>
          This journal is the field manual for that journey. From zero to monetization, bypassing the "junior developer" trap by using AI correctly.
        </p>
        
        <div class="my-16 p-8 border-l-4 border-accent bg-accent/5 italic">
          "AI is just a fast junior developer. You need to be the Senior Architect from day one."
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-3xl font-serif italic text-ink mt-12 mb-6">The Castaway Ethos</h3>
        <p>
          I'm an INTP. I live by feel. Andrej Karpathy called it "Vibe Coding." I just call it survival.
        </p>
        <p>
          I've built stock screeners that scan thousands of stocks and agents that collect massive datasets. All with zero CS degree.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-serif italic text-ink mt-12 mb-6">What you'll find here</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Field Reports:</strong> Real scars from building production-grade tools.</li>
          <li><strong>Spec Kit:</strong> How to set deterministic boundaries so AI doesn't produce garbage.</li>
          <li><strong>Guru Insights:</strong> Opinionated takes on the shifting landscape of development.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="mt-20">
          <a href="/posts" class="bg-ink text-background px-8 py-4 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase font-black hover:bg-ink/90 transition-colors inline-block">
            Explore the Logs
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
